tasks.item.description:
A scheduled task that runs at startup or when you sign in. Switching it OFF only disables the task: nothing is deleted and you can turn it ON again.
• Task · {name}
• Command · {command}

tasks.item.protected.description:
A scheduled task that runs at startup or when you sign in. Switching it OFF only disables the task: nothing is deleted and you can turn it ON again. Security, VPN and driver tasks may stop working properly. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Task · {name}
• Command · {command}

startup.source.run_user:
Starts when you sign in to Windows. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but it stays installed and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · your account

startup.source.run_machine:
Starts when any user signs in to Windows. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but it stays installed and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · all users

startup.source.folder_user:
Starts from your Startup folder. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but the shortcut stays and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · your Startup folder

startup.source.folder_machine:
Starts from the Startup folder of all users. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but the shortcut stays and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · all users' Startup folder

startup.source.service:
A background service that starts with Windows. Task Manager does not list it in Startup. Switching it OFF sets it to Manual, so it stops starting by itself but can still be started when something needs it. Security, VPN and database services may stop working properly. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}

startup.source.service_updater:
An updater service that starts with Windows. Switching it OFF sets it to Manual, so it stops starting by itself but can still run when something needs it. Updates for that software may arrive later.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}

apps.update.item.description:
Updates this app with winget, silently, from the version installed now to the latest. Some installers ask for administrator rights, and the app may be closed first.
• Name · {name}
• ID · {id}
• Current · {version}
• Latest · {available}

store.repair.item.description:
Registers the app again from its own files, without touching its data. If it still fails, try resetting it.
• Package · {name}
• Version · {version}

store.reset.item.description:
Deletes the local data and settings of the app and leaves it as freshly installed. Data kept in the cloud (your account) is not touched. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Package · {name}
• Version · {version}

programs.item.description:
Opens the program's own uninstaller, after you confirm. The uninstaller does the work and may ask for administrator rights itself. When it closes, Caduceus checks that the program is gone. Leftover files and registry entries are not touched.
• Name · {name}
• Publisher · {publisher}
• Version · {version}
• Installed · {installed}
• Uninstaller · {command}

programs.item.protected.description:
Opens the program's own uninstaller, after you confirm. Windows or other programs depend on drivers, runtimes and redistributables, so removing one can break them. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Name · {name}
• Publisher · {publisher}
• Version · {version}
